    "coil": {
      "description": "winding up. The tail throws most of its own length forward and every ring fattens as it goes, hardest where the pile-up is worst, so the body does not merely shorten — it thickens into itself. The head draws back against the arrival and takes its mouth with it; the mouth opens the way a ring of teeth does, spreading and turning off a throat that never changes size. The organ rides the ring it sits on and does nothing else — it is a scent organ, not a muscle. Wound rather than eased: a fast first draw, a slow creep against the load, a last snatch. It holds on the final frame, because the release is the dash.",
